Slice 050d, `tln tool update talon --from-source` on Windows (R-ST10, R-ST9, R-S2). The fake machine is `os=windows arch=x64`. The bin dir of Windows is `<USERPROFILE>\.local\bin`: the dir `u<n>\.local\bin` (a name with `\`) in the home. One home for each run (`HOME` and `USERPROFILE` are `{w}/home/u<n>`). The installed Talon is the prebuilt 0.3.1: the data file `tln.exe` and the entry `tln.exe` of the bin dir have the same text (Talon's, R-ST11). Home u1 also has the entry `roc.exe` (the same text), home u2 has no `roc.exe`. The rest is the home of `tool/ts6-source` run 1 (the tag v0.3.4, the commit `d0d0d0d0...`, one build). `fx/random` is not set, so every `random!` gives `0123456789abcdef`.

| Run | Home | Words | Result | Rules |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | u1 | `tool update talon --from-source` | the same calls as `tool/ts6-source` run 1 up to the build. The install under the lock renames the data file `tln.exe` and the entry `tln.exe` to `tln.0123456789abcdef.del` (050c, `ToolBuild.install!`). Then the entry `roc.exe` is made again: it exists, so after the `random!` of its temp name there is one more `random!` and `rename!` of `roc.exe` to `roc.0123456789abcdef.del`, before the hard link to the temp name and the `rename!` over `roc.exe`. The 3 `.del` files stay in the tree (the next start deletes them) | R-ST10, R-ST9, R-S2, R-T22 |
| 2 | u2 | `tool update talon --from-source` | `roc.exe` is not there: the entry is made (it is in `made`, the verdict is `Make` for an entry that is absent) with no `.del` rename and no second `random!`. Exit 0. Only the 2 `.del` files of `tln.exe` are in the tree | R-ST10, R-ST9, D8 |

Each run starts with the sweep of the `.del` files (`env_all` and one `list_dirs` of the 2 dirs, no `.del` file at the start, so no `delete`).
